# UI density (TradeDash)

User preference (repeated): status/connection strips must stay **one line**, concise, minimal blank space.

## Status / connection chips
- Layout: **dot above, short label below** — no metrics beside the dot
- Metrics (uptime, call counts, expiry, cache age) → **Radix `Tooltip`**, never bare `title=` (parent `overflow-hidden` / Electron often breaks native tooltips)
- Pack chips with `flex-nowrap gap-x-1` (or tighter); avoid `min-w-*`, large `gap-x-2+`, `flex-wrap` that pushes actions (e.g. Re-auth) to a second row
- Prefer short labels (FS, FH, Poly); full name lives in the tooltip
- Section chrome: small padding (`px-2 py-1.5`), short section word (“Conn” not a banner)

## Copy
- Dates: `M/D` or `M/D Ha` — not full `toLocaleString`
- Drop filler (“cache”, “ready”, “Pacific-day…”) when color already conveys state
- One strip > stacked banners for the same health signal

